12. Trade-offs
Simplicity over infra sophistication: local vector index instead of managed vector DB — faster to
stand up, easier for an evaluator to run in one command, at the cost of retrieval scale/quality ceiling.
Explicit refusal over confident guessing: the assistant will say “I don’t have that in the
transcripts” rather than blend model knowledge with retrieved knowledge — reduces perceived
helpfulness in edge cases but directly serves the “avoid hallucination” requirement.
Iframe sandboxing over rich HTML features: artifact viewer blocks scripts by default — safer,
but generated HTML artifacts can’t be interactive (no JS execution) unless a future iteration adds a

vetted allowlist.
13. Implementation Plan
See architecture.md for full technical detail. Summary sequence: Backend skeleton (FastAPI, sessions,
DB) → Ingestion/RAG → Agent + skills (grounded Q&A, Ship30, artifacts) → Frontend (chat + Artifact
Viewer) → Docker Compose + config/fallback → Tests → Documentation
